						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">Progression is linear.&nbsp; There are no side steps. <br /></div><br />That&#039;s silly, progression has had &quot;side steps&quot; since kunark.&nbsp; I&#039;m not sure how long you&#039;ve been around but I&#039;m sure you&#039;ve done PoP.&nbsp; Once you access Air/Earth/Water, you have a significant side step, either do SolRo for Fire, or work on those three.<br /><br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">It doesn&#039;t make them the top guild on the server, but it does put them first in progression.<br /></div><br />Only if you are equal in progression up to that point, and the target you killed was somehow more difficult than previous progression.&nbsp; <br /><br />As an example...<br />Guild A did all of Luclin but VT, and whacks Grummus...<br />Guild B did all of Luclin and VT, did not whack Grummus...<br /><br />You skipped a large chunk of content to do something the other guild could obviously do.&nbsp; It&#039;s like running a race, you don&#039;t get to skip lap 3 of 4 and get to claim you win.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">And for the record, no, I don&#039;t have balls, nor do I have any plans to grow them...<br /></div>You also don&#039;t have a yellow-stripe running down your back, but you know what the symbolism means.<br /><br /><div class="quoteheader">Quote</div><div class="quote">however, I don&#039;t hide behind fake names.&nbsp; My game name (and gender...) are on the left of my post.<br /></div><br />Last I checked my name was not fake, and your gender is irrelevant.</td>
