						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left">Maybe this game drastically changed from PoP but...<br /><br />I&#039;d pretty much have to completely disagree with the concept that the &quot;players&quot; win not the strat.&nbsp; EQ has always had a holy trinity of raiding.&nbsp; Players, Gear, Strategy.<br /><br />Take away one, and the other two simply aren&#039;t enough to get you by unless you go to an extreme(zerg/old content).&nbsp; If anything, the strat is the most important of the three, because it can be refined down to be as efficient as possible, thereby requiring less of the other two.<br /><br />The players &quot;win&quot; by not screwing up and following the strat correctly.&nbsp; Usually there is a finite core, 10-20% of the people on your raids who simply can&#039;t screw up, the rest of the people probably can and you will still, likely win.<br /><br />SoE made the game &quot;harder&quot; by forcing you to expand that core over the years.&nbsp; Emp Ssraa, Terris Thule, Xeg, Coirnav, Rathe... all are good examples.&nbsp; Each had it&#039;s own unique way of screwing with you, but the end goal was to make more of your raid force part of that &quot;core&quot; group.<br /><br />Everything else is really just the numbers, you need X dps, X healing, X mana regen, ect.<br /><br />Like Chubz alluded to, there really is only one &quot;right&quot; way to do an encounter usually.&nbsp; The right way is always the way that requires the least people/gear to be successful.<br /><br />That ties in with why Teir1 guilds guard strats so ferverently.&nbsp; See when they do an encounter the margin of error from the &quot;right&quot; way is very small, because the encounter is &quot;tuned&quot; for characters with their gear.&nbsp; If you show up an expansion or two later, your margin of error is going to be a hell of a lot bigger, so you have more room for &quot;slop&quot; in your strat, making life easier.&nbsp; Just like playing poker with an extra card...except in this game, it&#039;s levels or AA&#039;s.</td>
